    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk that feels a bit soft for the tone i'm going for. it's a bit too \"polite\" and doesn't really bite. it's more like a \"friendly observation\" than actual dark satire. can we lean into it more? like, instead of just saying \"we all live together,\" make it more about how the neighborhood perceives them—maybe something about how the neighbors think it's a constant party or some chaotic thing is always happening because of how many people are in the house. something that really leans into that \"unpredictable/chaotic\" trope to show how absurd the neighbors' assumptions are.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
